{"eligibility":"exclude","exclusion_criterion":"EC5","side_list":"correctness-only","eligibility_reason":"SynthCoder is a training technique (anti-pattern-aware masking, SFT and DPO) for LLM FIM code completion, but its outcomes are correctness or similarity metrics (EM, ES, Pass@1) plus code-echo ratio and generated-token length. These are inference-cost and usability measures, not readability, maintainability, runtime/memory efficiency or security of the generated code.","title":"SynthCoder: Anti-pattern identification and model training for FIM mode code completion","year":2025,"venue":"Empirical Software Engineering","venue_type":"","study_type":"","techniques":"","compute_reported":"","contamination_handled":"","human_eval":"","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"","reimplementable":"","qa":"","confidence":"medium","notes":"Borderline case. Mean generation length is called 'efficiency' by the authors, but it measures inference tokens, not the runtime efficiency of the generated code. Code-echo ratio is an erroneous-repetition defect rate, not an NF quality dimension as defined for this review."}
