{"eligibility":"exclude","exclusion_criterion":"EC4","side_list":"adjacent","eligibility_reason":"The study applies an iterative SonarQube-guided LLM loop to refactor existing human-written Java classes (Commons Lang, Commons IO, Guava). That makes it LLM refactoring of human code, not improvement of LLM-generated code.","title":"An Empirical Study on the Effectiveness of Iterative LLM-Based Improvements for Static Analysis Issues","year":2025,"venue":"SBES '25 (Brazilian Symposium on Software Engineering)","venue_type":"","study_type":"","techniques":"","compute_reported":"","contamination_handled":"","human_eval":"","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"","reimplementable":"","qa":"","confidence":"medium","notes":"Borderline under IC2: the code is 'edited by an LLM', but the edits apply to human-written repositories. This is the exact case the 'adjacent' side list defines. Reported outcomes are SonarQube issue counts and technical debt (maintainability); correctness was checked only manually. Artifacts are on Zenodo (doi:10.5281/zenodo.15278368)."}
```

