{"eligibility":"include","exclusion_criterion":"","side_list":"none","eligibility_reason":"A role-prompt template plus an error/validity feedback loop is applied to five LLMs to rewrite existing TSP algorithm code. The LLM-edited code is evaluated quantitatively for runtime (Branch and Bound) and cyclomatic complexity (Radon). This is borderline: the edited code is human-written, and the baseline is the original code rather than an LLM without the technique.","title":"Combinatorial Optimization for All: Using LLMs to Aid Non-Experts in Improving Optimization Algorithms","year":2026,"venue":"Inteligencia Artificial, 29(77)","venue_type":"peer-reviewed-journal","study_type":"technique-evaluation","techniques":[{"technique_name":"Role-prompted algorithm improvement template with interactive execution-error/invalid-solution refinement","family_v0":"prompting","stage":"pre-generation","signal_source":["test-execution","human"],"tools":"Radon (cyclomatic complexity); irace for parameter tuning","iterations":"Repeated until valid code is obtained, with temperature lowered each retry; up to 4 attempts observed (Table 3)","dims_targeted":["efficiency"],"dims_measured":["efficiency","readability-maintainability"],"correctness_measured":true,"metrics":"efficiency: runtime of Branch and Bound codes [execution]; readability-maintainability: cyclomatic complexity [tool-static, Radon]; solution quality: TSP tour length [execution]","benchmarks":"pyCombinatorial, 10 algorithms; TSPLib, 10 instances (rat99 to vm1084); 10 random 10-15 city instances for Branch and Bound","languages":"Python","models":"Claude-3.5-Sonnet (closed, instruct); Gemini-exp-1206 (closed); Llama-3.3-70B (open, instruct); GPT-o1 (closed, reasoning); DeepSeek-R1 (open, reasoning)","baselines":"Original pyCombinatorial human-written implementations","effect_target":"mixed","effect_target_headline":"","effect_correctness":"mixed","effect_correctness_headline":"LLM-enhanced code versions clearly outperformed the original implementations in nine out of ten cases/algorithms","effect_other_dims":{"readability-maintainability":"mixed","efficiency":"targeted","security":"NR"}}],"compute_reported":["calls"],"contamination_handled":"no","human_eval":"none","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"https://camilochs.github.io/comb-opt-for-all/","reimplementable":"yes","qa":{"QA1":1,"QA2":0.5,"QA3":1,"QA4":1,"QA5":1,"QA6":0.5,"QA7":0.5,"QA8":1,"QA9":0,"QA10":0.5},"confidence":"low","notes":"Eligibility is borderline (could arguably be classed as adjacent: LLM editing of human code). Runtime is measured only for Branch and Bound: o1 and R1 were faster than the original, the other models slower. Average cyclomatic complexity: original 6.95 vs. Claude 5.60, o1 6.84, Gemini 7.34, Llama 7.38, R1 7.51. Statistical significance is mentioned but no tests are detailed. Tables are garbled."}
```

