{"eligibility":"exclude","exclusion_criterion":"EC4","side_list":"adjacent","eligibility_reason":"Based on the abstract only, Nemesis is a multi-agent LLM framework that finds vulnerabilities in existing open-source codebases and patches them. This is vulnerability discovery and repair of human-written code, not improvement of LLM-generated code. It is borderline because the patches are LLM-edited code with a 'Patch Robustness' outcome.","title":"Nemesis: An Adversarial Multi-Agent AI Framework for Proactive Vulnerability Discovery and Patch Synthesis","year":2026,"venue":"2026 International Conference on Emerging Trends and Innovations in ICT (ICEI)","venue_type":"","study_type":"","techniques":[],"compute_reported":[],"contamination_handled":"","human_eval":"","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"","reimplementable":"","qa":{},"confidence":"low","notes":"Only the abstract was available. A reviewer should check the full text for how Patch Robustness is measured. If the security of the LLM-synthesized patches is quantified, as LLM-edited code, the paper could arguably meet IC2/IC3 and be included under the multi-agent family."}
